<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-8339] After cluster activation actual partition state restored from WAL may be lost</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8339</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;On cluster activation we restore partition states from checkpoint and WAL. But before that action we pre-create partitions by ideal assignment on &quot;beforeExchange&quot; phase and own it in case of first or next activation. This partition state change is logged to WAL and override actual last state of partition during restore.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible solutions:&lt;br/&gt;
1) Pre-create partitions after actual restore.&lt;br/&gt;
2) Do not log to WAL partition own on pre-create phase.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
